# Copy to `.env` for local development. `.env` is gitignored; this file is the
# template, and the only variable in it is the one below.
#
# WHAT THIS IS NOT: production. The deployed app gets `VITE_SYNC_URL` from the
# Cloudflare Pages project's environment variables, not from a file in the repo,
# and the *Worker* gets its own address from `wrangler.jsonc`'s `routes`. Those
# two are the opposite ends of the same wire — where the Worker answers, and
# where the app dials — and nothing links them automatically. This file exists
# so that on your own machine they can point somewhere else entirely.
#
# The usual reason to have a `.env` at all: run `pnpm sync:dev` and you get a
# throwaway sync backend on localhost, so you can pair two browser profiles and
# watch them converge without touching real data. That is what the default below
# is for.
#
# Point it at https://sapling-sync.vanoverloop.xyz instead to run the local app
# against the real backend — which also means the real library, so be deliberate
# about it.
#
# Unset entirely, the app has no sync at all: no network code is reachable and
# Settings says so. That is the default and a supported configuration.
#
# It has to be a build-time variable rather than a setting, because the module
# that needs it is the LiveStore leader worker, and a Web Worker has no
# localStorage to read one from (`src/lib/sync/url.ts`). Being build-time also
# means changing it never affects a build that already exists — including the
# deployed one, which needs a fresh Pages build to pick up a change.
VITE_SYNC_URL=http://localhost:8787
